  "scope": "The Kitty Unicode placeholder grid suite alone in one persistent (KeepOnClose, image policy 5) tab on a disposable macOS sidecar: two cases (the tile rows, the row marks and the inheritance of a nonzero row on a 4 x 2 grid; and tiles that scroll, shrink and grow with their text rows), over paired original offscreen PNGs and complete cells/modes. No stock collector ran, so there is no stock grade and no Core or common-harness claim; the pinned callbacks are replayed from the retained bundle and stay inconclusive by design. Not measured: an ordinary (non-persistent) tab in this publication (see the ordinary-tab one), a grid whose aspect differs from the image's (where the image sits inside the grid is not asserted: a cell is read where its quadrant is under every placement of the square), swapped columns on a grid, ids above 24 bits (the third diacritic), relative placements (P=, Q=), resize and reflow of placeholder cells, a palette or theme background behind the cells, text selection and copy, a second client, remote persistent sessions, other platforms, a restart or reattach with placeholders on screen.",
