      "effectContract": {
        "id": "ntilde-kitty-unicode-placeholder-grid-persistent-effect-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "statement": "In a persistent tab (persistent image policy 5), Kitty Unicode placeholders behave as the Kitty protocol specifies over a grid of more than one row, read by paired offscreen captures of a 4 x 2 grid of cells: a transmitted 16x16 image in four colored quadrants (red and green above, blue and yellow below) with a virtual placement (a=p,U=1) of a 4 x 2 grid draws nothing by itself; cells whose row and column marks name the grid's tiles show the quadrant color of their tile (red red green green over blue blue yellow yellow); the row marks and not the screen row choose the tile (the rows swapped on screen swap their colors, and the lower tiles printed on the top screen row alone show blue and yellow there with nothing below); a placeholder without marks after a cell with marks (row 1, column 0 in the lower row) continues in the same row at the next column, so a nonzero row is inherited too; and tiles belong to the text that carries them: scrolling the screen up one line moves them up with their cells, erasing the lower text row removes the lower tiles and only them, and inserting a line above the grid moves them down. A line a terminal scrolls in or inserts holds either the active background or the default cell depending on the terminal, and the suite accepts both. Every command that expects a Kitty reply returned OK (the virtual placement's reply echoes its placement id), and each clear passed its fence and left its target blank.",
        "primary": "https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/graphics-protocol/#unicode-placeholders",
        "carrierCases": [
          "kitty.placeholders.rows",
          "kitty.placeholders.scroll"
        ],
